<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wihwa Island</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Wihwado</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wihwa Island is an island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yalu-river">Yalu River</a> near modern Sinuiju, on the border between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-korea">North Korea</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. In 1388 the Goryeo general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taejo-of-joseon">Yi Seong-gye</a>, sent to attack Ming forces in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a>, halted there and turned his army back to the capital. The retreat from Wihwa Island led to his seizure of power and the founding of the Joseon dynasty in 1392.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wihwa-island.jpg" alt="Wihwa Island" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sinuiju_124.39213E_40.10175N.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
